description:
## Goal

Move the remaining current non-coverage warning producer, `type/numeric-literal-widened`, onto the final typed warning-evidence and retained-diagnostic model, make type resolution side-effect-free, and delete the global warning queue/flush lifecycle.

## Model

A resolver computes types; it must not mutate a World warning accumulator or emit telemetry. Its result returns typed warning observations alongside the resolved value/error. The exact demanded caller job folds those observations into its ordinary `AttemptOutcome`/`JobEffects` contribution.

Census and migrate every production resolver entry point, including `DeriveTypeDef`, `DeriveFunctionContract`, guard/type-pattern planning, and extern/body signature resolution. No caller may silently discard observations or preserve the old side effect.

A numeric-literal warning identity uses the source-owned declaration plus a stable typed path within the type expression. It does not use `Span::DUMMY`, diagnostic text, rendered literals, or encounter order. Exact source-version provenance supplies the current span. Reproduction replaces the owning attempt contribution; loss of demand or accepted-source replacement retracts it; independent ordinary contributors preserve equal evidence.

The retained diagnostic snapshot from fz-kdt.36.1 reads this evidence through exact product/fact/provenance dependencies. A cached unchanged request returns the same allocation/generation without rerunning resolution; unrelated edits move nothing.

## TDD

Prove first for every production resolver context:

- first demanded numeric-literal resolution publishes one typed warning observation/fact and one rendered warning at the real source span;
- an undemanded declaration stays cold and produces no work, fact, diagnostic, or dependency;
- identical requests preserve evidence and snapshot allocation/generation with zero jobs, evaluations, wakes, allocations, copies, or producer telemetry;
- relevant replacement removes, moves, or restores the warning exactly;
- rejected replacement preserves the accepted warning and provenance;
- two demanders preserve equal evidence until the last ordinary support leaves;
- location-only replacement changes provenance/snapshot only;
- FIFO, LIFO, and permutation are identical.

## Required deletion

Delete `World.reported_warnings`, `World.warning_diagnostics`, `WarningDiagnosticKey`, `clear_reported_warnings`, `note_warning_once`, `emit_warning_once`, `flush_reported_warnings`, every drive/product-drive warning flush, and resolver-to-World warning side effects. Warning delivery is not a queue drain, emitter side effect, retry registry, whole-World scan, or second ProductMemo. Keep `Diagnostic` as immutable presentation data, not semantic authority.

Update resolver, diagnostic, fact-engine, pipeline, telemetry, and user-facing documentation in the same commit. Full focused, causal, replacement, fixture, CLI, formatting, check, and strict-Clippy gates pass.
